  <data key="d7">{"finding": "This cycle tested hybrid_d_gaf_attention_cnn.py on 2D_CWT_SCALOGRAM (SERS_data_test) with three configs: (num_conv_layers=4, filters=128, lr=1e-4, dropout=0.2) gave HO=0.6722; (num_conv_layers=6, filters=64, lr=5e-5, dropout=0.3) gave HO=0.7811 and 0.7463. Crucially, none explicitly passed batch_norm=1, so the default batch_norm=0 was active. The best HO (0.7811) is far below the standard architecture's best (0.8467). Conclusion: this hybrid architecture requires batch_norm=1 to be viable; future tests must include it. No progress on breaking the ~0.84 ceiling.", "category": "architecture_performance", "experiment_name": "hybrid_d_gaf_attention_cnn.py", "_data_source": "SERS_data_test", "_manifest_name": "SERS_data_test", "_dataset_params": {"n_fft": 1024, "hop_length": 512, "gaf_image_size": 32, "video_num_segments": 1, "video_gaf_image_size": 32, "representation_type": "2D_GAF"}}</data>
