<edge source="resnetd_gaf_video_enhanced.py_6bfefb2a" target="resnetd_gaf_video_enhanced.py_6bfefb2a" id="memorize_finding(finding=Consolidated summary at step 48 (for th...)">
  <data key="d3">memorize_finding(finding=Consolidated summary at step 48 (for th...)</data>
  <data key="d4">1</data>
  <data key="d5">[-0.05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]</data>
  <data key="d6">[[-0.05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]]</data>
  <data key="d7">{"finding": "Consolidated summary at step 48 (for the last block of research):\n## Strategic Lesson for Next Optimization Phase\n\n### What to Keep\n- **Architecture direction:** Larger models with more conv layers (5\u20136), larger filters (100\u2013130), larger kernels (5), and moderate dense units (200\u2013250).  \n- **Optimization settings:** Lower learning rate (~0.0007), smaller batch size (16), higher weight decay (~0.00035), and moderate dropout (~0.30).  \n- **Validation metric:** Use **heldout accuracy** as the primary target (it is nearly identical to mean accuracy, so track only one).\n\n### What to Change\n- **Separate transfer learning workflows:** Trials with `freeze_depth`, `mixup_alpha`, or pretraining delta must be analyzed separately. Their poor performance (worst trials) confounds architecture conclusions.  \n- **Overfitting as primary constraint:** The 7.5% train-accuracy gap in best trials is unacceptable. Explicitly minimize `overfitting_score` or train-validation gap.  \n- **Validation methodology:** Use independent validation splits (not the same data used for correlation analysis) to avoid metric redundancy and overfitting to the heldout set.  \n- **Evaluation:** Replace single-trial comparisons with percentile-based or clustered failure modes (e.g., underfitting, overfitting, poor transfer).  \n- **Regularization mix:** Increase dropout beyond 0.30 and explore data augmentation (mixup_alpha) *for non-transfer trials* \u2013 it was non-significant only in one setting. Consider early stopping (patience &gt;20) actively.\n\n### New Hypothesis\n&gt; **Deep, high-capacity CNNs can achieve &gt;0.90 heldout accuracy only when combined with strong regularization that closes the train-validation gap.**  \n&gt; The key is not just larger models or lower learning rates, but a **balanced trade-off** between capacity and overfitting control. Transfer learning (pretraining+finetune) introduces its own failure modes (negative delta) and should be treated as a separate hyperparameter branch.  \n&gt; **Next objective:** Minimize `overfitting_score` (train \u2013 heldout accuracy) to &lt;3% while maintaining heldout accuracy &gt;0.88, using a unified validation set and controlling for pretraining status.", "experiment_name": "resnetd_gaf_video_enhanced.py", "_data_source": "SERS_data_test", "_manifest_name": "SERS_data_test", "_dataset_params": {"n_fft": 1024, "hop_length": 512, "gaf_image_size": 32, "video_num_segments": 1, "video_gaf_image_size": 32, "representation_type": "2D_GAF"}}</data>
  <data key="d8">[-0.05450000000000001, 0.0003261062335968018, 0.00044317683469165584, 1.759973553657532, 0.3321544063568116]</data>
</edge>
