  <data key="d7">{"finding": "Confirmed architectural ceiling for optimized_d_gaf_cnn.py on SERS_data_test: dropout=0.4, batch_norm=1, kernel_size=5 gave mean_heldout=0.8761, mean_overfitting_score=0.0955 \u2014 virtually identical to last cycle's 0.8764. Structural regularization (high dropout, batch_norm, L2) does NOT compress the train-validation gap, confirming the plateau is a hard architectural boundary, not a hyperparameter issue. Abandon tuning; next cycle must pivot to architectural redesign.", "category": "architectural_ceiling", "experiment_name": "optimized_d_gaf_cnn.py", "_data_source": "SERS_data_test", "_manifest_name": "SERS_data_test", "_dataset_params": {"n_fft": 512, "hop_length": 64, "gaf_image_size": 48, "video_num_segments": 8, "video_gaf_image_size": 24, "representation_type": "2D_GAF"}}</data>
