  <data key="d5">[-0.05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]</data>
  <data key="d6">[[-0.05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], [-0.05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]]</data>
  <data key="d7">{"finding": "Cycle summary for 1D_CNN/2D_CWT_SCALOGRAM on SERS_data_test: O1 isolated kernel_size=7 with lr=0.00003, dropout=0.6, batch_norm=1 \u2014 HO=0.643, shifted=0.333, proving the kernel alone isn't the root cause of 1D_CNN underperformance. O2 finetune (ft_unfreeze_last_n=2, ft_lr=3e-5) collapsed pretrain HO=0.839\u21920.360 (delta=-0.48), shifted=0.599 \u2014 still catastrophic forgetting. O3 confirmed shifted=0.599. O4 switched to 2D_CWT_SCALOGRAM. O5: 2D_CWT_SCALOGRAM with num_conv_layers=4, filters=64, kernel_size=3, lr=0.0001 achieved HO=0.820, and with filters=128, kernel_size=5, lr=5e-5, dropout=0.5 achieved HO=0.850 \u2014 both well above 0.82 target. However shifted_test remained low (0.31-0.34), likely needing finetune on the shifted distribution. 1D_CNN flag: abandoned_underperforming \u2014 7+ trials with consistent shifted stagnation below 0.60. 2D_CWT_SCALOGRAM shows strong HO performance and is the recommended path forward with finetune escalation.", "category": "abandonment", "experiment_name": "2D_CWT_SCALOGRAM", "_data_source": "SERS_data_test", "_manifest_name": "SERS_data_test", "_dataset_params": {}}</data>
  <data key="d8">[-0.058955000000000014, 0.03793818374728562, 0.011448325864219453, 2.247312378145695, 8.300539291411974]</data>
</edge>
