<edge source="2D_CWT_SCALOGRAM_a4b99764" target="2D_CWT_SCALOGRAM_a4b99764" id="memorize_finding(finding=2D_CWT_SCALOGRAM finetune breakthrough ...)">
  <data key="d3">memorize_finding(finding=2D_CWT_SCALOGRAM finetune breakthrough ...)</data>
  <data key="d4">2</data>
  <data key="d5">[-0.05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]</data>
  <data key="d6">[[-0.05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], [-0.05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]]</data>
  <data key="d7">{"finding": "2D_CWT_SCALOGRAM finetune breakthrough on SERS_data_test: O1 generalization gap 0.1586 (&gt;0.15 target, not met). O2 sweep lr 1e-5\u21925e-4 best HO=0.7615 (trial 3: lr=1.35e-5, dropout=0.34, filters=64, kernel=7). O3 with num_conv_layers=3, lr=2e-5: HO=0.785, shifted=0.311 \u2014 still low shifted despite strong HO. O4 sweep confirmed low-lr region doesn't lift shifted. O5 finetune (ft_unfreeze_last_n=3, ft_lr=3e-5, ft_backbone_lr_scale=0.1) is the critical win: pretrain HO=0.879 \u2192 finetune HO=0.370 (held-out forgetting) BUT shifted_test soared from ~0.31 to 0.737 (+0.43 improvement). Per-class shifted: Citrobacter 0.784, E.coli 0.812, Enterococcus 0.615. Distribution gap compressed to -0.367 (shifted now exceeds held-out, meaning finetune successfully realigned wavelet features to the target domain). Partial backbone unfreezing is the correct strategy for 2D_CWT_SCALOGRAM shifted-domain adaptation.", "category": "breakthrough", "experiment_name": "2D_CWT_SCALOGRAM", "_data_source": "SERS_data_test", "_manifest_name": "SERS_data_test", "_dataset_params": {}}</data>
  <data key="d8">[-0.058955000000000014, 0.04562911954359771, 0.00997945206492614, 1.6127169104089738, 0.3113019794002534]</data>
</edge>
