  <data key="d7">{"finding": "hybrid_d_gaf_attention_cnn.py on 3D_DYNAMIC_GAF (SERS_data_test): Systematic finetune freeze-depth sweep (ft_unfreeze_last_n=0,3,4,6) shows head-only finetuning (n=0) achieves best shifted_test_accuracy=0.571, while deeper unfreezing monotonically degrades shifted domain alignment (n=3\u21920.490, n=4\u21920.405, n=6\u21920.399). However, all finetunes show catastrophic finetune HO collapse (0.28-0.61 vs pretrain 0.89-0.90), indicating the finetune split distribution does not match the test distribution. The pretrained features are useful for the shifted domain (head-only shifted 0.571 &gt; chance 0.333) but unfreezing destroys them. The +0.167 session shift gap cannot be closed via patient-unfreezing for this architecture. Recommend switching to 3D_WAVELET_CWT or 2D_CWT_SCALOGRAM representations which achieved shifted_test 0.687-0.712 with fewer trials.", "category": "architecture", "experiment_name": "hybrid_d_gaf_attention_cnn.py", "_data_source": "SERS_data_test", "_manifest_name": "SERS_data_test", "_dataset_params": {}}</data>
  <data key="d8">[-0.058955000000000014, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]</data>
</edge>
